WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.256
Welcome to the last chapter of
Building Global Secure Access,

2
00:00:04.256 --> 00:00:07.225
Chapter 9: deploying to
test and production.

3
00:00:07.225 --> 00:00:10.837
The labs proved the code on
fixtures and in a test tenant.

4
00:00:10.837 --> 00:00:15.341
This runbook moves the rollout itself:
one ring at a time, logs first,

5
00:00:15.341 --> 00:00:20.173
emergency access checked before
anything changes, every change from a

6
00:00:20.173 --> 00:00:24.676
plan a second person approved, and
a go or no-go from measured values.

7
00:00:24.676 --> 00:00:27.798
It hasn't been run against a live tenant;

8
00:00:27.798 --> 00:00:33.610
the output you'll see is the kit's
fixture mode, run on November 17, 2026.

9
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.410
Why a runbook?

10
00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.323
Because the order is the safety.

11
00:00:40.323 --> 00:00:44.526
Before you start: every chapter's
Lab 2 has run in a test tenant,

12
00:00:44.526 --> 00:00:47.048
with its findings fixed or recorded.

13
00:00:47.048 --> 00:00:51.186
The decision records are approved
for every function the ring enables.

14
00:00:51.186 --> 00:00:53.685
The network diagnostic setting exists.

15
00:00:53.685 --> 00:00:57.246
The emergency access accounts
exist and have been tested,

16
00:00:57.246 --> 00:00:59.323
from Building Privileged Access.

17
00:00:59.323 --> 00:01:02.174
Microsoft's break-glass
scripts for compliant

18
00:01:02.174 --> 00:01:04.734
network outages are staged and rehearsed.

19
00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:08.596
And the change record is open,
because Learn treats enabling a new

20
00:01:08.596 --> 00:01:12.385
traffic profile as a major change
for the change advisory board.

21
00:01:12.385 --> 00:01:17.160
Roles are activated through privileged
identity management for the window only.

22
00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:25.396
Step 1 is one settings file per
environment, copied from the template,

23
00:01:25.396 --> 00:01:29.409
with every placeholder filled:
the tenant, the ring, the groups,

24
00:01:29.409 --> 00:01:33.580
the Intune application IDs, the
security profile, the workspace,

25
00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:37.436
the in-scope device count from
Intune, the minimum versions,

26
00:01:37.436 --> 00:01:41.922
the acceptable-use categories, and
the authentication authorities.

27
00:01:41.922 --> 00:01:46.860
The settings hold names and IDs only;
the operator signs in as a person.

28
00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:51.568
The kit refuses a file with anything
that looks like a secret, a test or

29
00:01:51.568 --> 00:01:56.772
production file with a placeholder left
in it, and any cloud but GCC or global.

30
00:01:56.772 --> 00:02:00.513
Everything after this is the
same command for both stages;

31
00:02:00.513 --> 00:02:04.460
only the file, the evidence
folder and the tenant change.

32
00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:11.487
Step 2 signs in to the
stage's tenant, collects,

33
00:02:11.487 --> 00:02:14.410
and runs the preflight, which only reads.

34
00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.485
Six checks.

35
00:02:15.485 --> 00:02:17.722
The settings file names this stage.

36
00:02:17.722 --> 00:02:21.872
The collection matches its manifest
and was read in the right tenant.

37
00:02:21.872 --> 00:02:25.623
The emergency access group is
excluded from every network

38
00:02:25.623 --> 00:02:28.685
policy in the tenant, not
just the ones in the plan.

39
00:02:28.685 --> 00:02:32.710
The network diagnostic setting
exists, so logs come before the ring.

40
00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:36.623
Every function the desired state
enables has an approved decision.

41
00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:39.859
And in production, the test
stage's evidence passes.

42
00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:44.708
Any failure stops the stage; the pilot
fixture fails the emergency check,

43
00:02:44.708 --> 00:02:48.060
because of the Finance
policy from Chapter 6.

44
00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:52.735
Who does what?

45
00:02:52.735 --> 00:02:56.165
The platform owner fills
the settings, collects,

46
00:02:56.165 --> 00:02:59.510
plans, applies, and does
the manual portal steps.

47
00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:02.046
A second person, from the change board,

48
00:03:02.046 --> 00:03:05.072
approves each plan's hash
and each rollback's.

49
00:03:05.072 --> 00:03:09.624
The policy owner approves the decision
records and the ring's desired state,

50
00:03:09.624 --> 00:03:13.959
and passes the enforce switch when a
policy's report-only period is clean.

51
00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:18.115
The technical program manager runs
the rings and keeps the ring record,

52
00:03:18.115 --> 00:03:20.510
and the service owner approves each exit.

53
00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:25.322
The security officer keeps each stage's
evidence folder, inside the boundary.

54
00:03:25.322 --> 00:03:27.560
No one approves their own change.

55
00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.835
Here's the fixture run, the
fictional tenant at ring 1.

56
00:03:34.835 --> 00:03:38.783
The preflight passes all five
test-stage checks: the right stage,

57
00:03:38.783 --> 00:03:43.698
a collection that matches its manifest
in the right tenant, the emergency group

58
00:03:43.698 --> 00:03:46.231
excluded from all five network policies,

59
00:03:46.231 --> 00:03:49.210
the diagnostic setting,
and approved decisions.

60
00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:52.820
Step 3 plans the rollback for
the state the ring starts from,

61
00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:57.830
before the ring starts: three enforced
policies to report-only in the guide's order,

62
00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:02.472
tagging off with the tenant restrictions
policy kept, then the manual steps.

63
00:04:02.472 --> 00:04:08.020
It's reviewed, its hash filed, and it's
applied only if a backout trigger fires.

64
00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:13.945
Step 4 is the staged enable.

65
00:04:13.945 --> 00:04:16.843
Plan the ring from its
reviewed desired state,

66
00:04:16.843 --> 00:04:19.970
have a second person approve
the hash, and apply it.

67
00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:24.645
Pass the enforce switch only for a policy
whose report-only period was clean.

68
00:04:24.645 --> 00:04:29.166
Then do the plan's manual steps: assign
the ring's group to each profile

69
00:04:29.166 --> 00:04:33.845
in the portal, and widen the Intune
client assignment in the same change.

70
00:04:33.845 --> 00:04:39.183
Step 5 comes after the ring's exit period:
collect again and run the smoke test.

71
00:04:39.183 --> 00:04:43.057
It runs every area's checks
and the ring exit criteria.

72
00:04:43.057 --> 00:04:46.387
In the fixture at ring
1, a hundred checks run,

73
00:04:46.387 --> 00:04:50.457
none fail, every criterion
passes, and the ring says go.

74
00:04:50.457 --> 00:04:54.310
Then run the guide's own Validate
steps for the ring's group.

75
00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:01.245
Step 6: backout triggers
are set before each ring,

76
00:05:01.245 --> 00:05:06.101
for example sign-in failures above the
baseline, help desk calls above the

77
00:05:06.101 --> 00:05:11.435
threshold, a mission application unreachable,
or TLS failures above one percent.

78
00:05:11.435 --> 00:05:16.395
When one fires, apply Step 3's rollback
with its approved hash, do its manual

79
00:05:16.395 --> 00:05:21.273
steps in order, and collect again so
the evidence shows the state after it.

80
00:05:21.273 --> 00:05:23.647
In Stage 1, rehearse it once.

81
00:05:23.647 --> 00:05:28.472
Step 7 records every run of the stage
and checks the stage's evidence.

82
00:05:28.472 --> 00:05:32.277
In the fixture, every file matches,
five records form a chain,

83
00:05:32.277 --> 00:05:35.772
and each step the test stage
needs has a passing record.

84
00:05:35.772 --> 00:05:40.550
Production also needs the telemetry
step, with CISA telemetry agreed.

85
00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.162
Step 8 is the go or no-go for production.

86
00:05:47.162 --> 00:05:50.384
It starts only when the test
stage's evidence passes,

87
00:05:50.384 --> 00:05:53.006
which the production preflight re-checks;

88
00:05:53.006 --> 00:05:56.377
the test tenant said go and
the rollback was rehearsed;

89
00:05:56.377 --> 00:06:00.646
the policy owner approved the
production records and desired state,

90
00:06:00.646 --> 00:06:03.193
and the change board approved the change;

91
00:06:03.193 --> 00:06:07.463
and CISA telemetry is agreed before
ring 3 retires the VPN's web path.

92
00:06:07.463 --> 00:06:12.087
Step 9 repeats Steps 2 to 7 in
production, one ring at a time.

93
00:06:12.087 --> 00:06:17.062
Its preflight takes the test evidence,
and in the fixture all six checks pass.

94
00:06:17.062 --> 00:06:19.494
For each later ring, change the ring,

95
00:06:19.494 --> 00:06:22.849
use its desired state and
widen the assignments.

96
00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:27.920
Remove a VPN route only after ten
business days with no traffic on it.

97
00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:36.310
The stage's evidence supports impact
analysis and contingency planning for the

98
00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:40.535
preflight, configuration change control
for the plans and the ring exits,

99
00:06:40.535 --> 00:06:43.374
the contingency plan for
the rehearsed rollback,

100
00:06:43.374 --> 00:06:46.283
and protection of audit
information for the chain.

101
00:06:46.283 --> 00:06:48.445
The assessor decides the controls.

102
00:06:48.445 --> 00:06:51.620
The dangers: changing a
ring before its logs exist,

103
00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:54.563
a policy that catches
the emergency accounts,

104
00:06:54.563 --> 00:06:59.286
a plan applied that differs from the
one reviewed, an improvised rollback,

105
00:06:59.286 --> 00:07:02.461
production before the test
evidence is complete,

106
00:07:02.461 --> 00:07:04.707
and unattended runs of the beta API.

107
00:07:04.707 --> 00:07:08.554
You're done when every stage's
preflight passed, the rollback was

108
00:07:08.554 --> 00:07:12.619
reviewed and rehearsed, and every
hash was approved by someone else.

109
00:07:12.619 --> 00:07:15.682
That's the end of Building
Global Secure Access.

110
00:07:15.682 --> 00:07:16.840
Thanks for watching.
